  "notes": "Inventory is the complete developer-facing surface defined by the specification of 4 March 2026: the document-level autofill event, the AutofillEvent interface (constructor + two readonly attributes), the RefillCallback callback type, the AutofillEventInit dictionary, the AutofillValueEntry typedef, and the new full-address autocomplete token. HTMLElement/DOMString/EventInit are external types, not feature surface. Known spec/explainer drift is disclosed on the page rather than resolved by invention: the explainer says the event does not bubble and names the property 'values' (with boolean entries for checkbox/radio), while the published spec sets bubbles=true and defines autofillValues with DOMString values; the pages document the spec. The spec's rendered IDL contains a bikeshed markup artifact on the autofillValues member lines; the page reproduces the IDL with the artifact removed and says so."
